<http://data.silknow.org/object/dca888ae-dac6-3a51-b413-d09f9b254b22/observation/2>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The pattern on this silk is 'Flower Garden'. On 4 March 1879 William Morris described it in a letter to a friend. He wrote, 'I am...in a whirlwind of dyeing and weaving, and...rather excited by a new piece...which looks beautiful, like a flower garden'.  Morris claims to have chosen the colours to 'suggest the beauties of inlaid metal'. They were almost certainly influenced by a display of items from Damascus he had studied in a dealer's shop in London in 1878.  This silk cost 19/6d (97.5p) in 1919 when the V&A acquired this sample."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/dca888ae-dac6-3a51-b413-d09f9b254b22> .

